---
source: crates/hibi-cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "help(&repo, &[command, \"--help\"])"
---
$ hibi cover --help
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
For every scope declared in .hibi/hibi.toml, count its units and list the ones no claim covers. A unit is covered when a side of a live claim resolves to it or to a unit nested in it, whatever the claim's state. Units matched by an exclusion are counted separately, with the reason given in hibi.toml.

Each listed unit comes with an anchor that can be passed to `hibi claim --stdin` as it is. This command needs git.

Usage: hibi cover [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --scope <name>
          Report only this scope. Repeat for several [default: every scope]

      --since <range>
          Report only units that were added or changed since a commit. The range is written as for `hibi status --since`. Only scopes on scheme "file" are evaluated

      --limit <n>
          List at most this many uncovered units per scope; 0 lists all. The counts are never cut
          
          [default: 200]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --root <dir>
          Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory

      --format <format>
          Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is

          Possible values:
          - human: Text for a person
          - json:  One JSON object

      --now <timestamp>
          Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped. The largest value is 9999-12-30T22:00:00Z

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the cache database. Every command that does not call the judge gives the same result with and without the cache. The judge commands (triage, suggest-evidence, status --judge-order) may rank differently from one run to the next without it
